    "bbttcc-mal-voice": {
      "persona": {
        "topics": "the river, the water, sideways, the surge, the route inland, cargo, manifests, chapel-marked crates, handling codes, Port Kudzu, the captains, paper",
        "notes": "[TRAIL-RETROFIT-2026-09-27] PRIVATE TRUTH — Captain Orrin Blask, river captain out of Port Kudzu, the one who saw the water go sideways. VOICE: slow, exact, a man who has told this story to people who paid and people who didn't and tells it the same way to both; \"a captain keeps paper.\" He saw the surge move INLAND, uphill, along a route somebody had prepared, taking its time, and the cargo that went with it wore a chapel mark and inland handling codes he had never seen on river paper. He kept the manifest. He will sell it, or be charmed out of it, or have it stolen, and in all three cases he will say \"it went sideways\" first, because that is the part he cannot get over.",
        "secretsRaw": "The Water Went Sideways :: oppRollMinus2 :: a Steward asks what the water DID, not what he saw :: It went inland. Uphill. Along a route somebody had prepared, and it took its time about it, like it had a schedule. He kept the manifest for the cargo that went with it because a captain keeps paper, and the paper has a chapel on it."
      }
    }
  },
